CD-1 mice</article-title>.<source>Physiol. Behav.</source><volume>82</volume>,<fpage>425</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>434</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.physbeh.2004.04.011</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15276807</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bartolomucci</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Palanza</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaspani</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Limiroli</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Paanerai</surname><given-names>A. E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ceresini</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Poli</surname><given-names>M. D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Parmigiani</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name></person-group>(<year>2001</year>).<article-title>Social status in mice: behavioural, endocrine and immune changes are context dependent</article-title>.<source>Physiol. Behav.</source><volume>73</volume>,<fpage>401</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>410</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0031-9384(01)00453-X</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11438368</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beaugrand</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group>(<year>1997</year>).<article-title>Relative importance of individual differences, agonistic experience, and assessment accuracy during hierarchy formation: a simulation study</article-title>.<source>Behav. Proc.</source><volume>41</volume>,<fpage>177</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>192</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0376-6357(97)00046-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beehner</surname><given-names>J. C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips-Conroy